# Copy to site/.env before building. .env is gitignored; .env.example is not.
#
# This file holds BUILD-TIME values only. Anything prefixed PUBLIC_ is inlined
# into the HTML by Astro and is visible to anyone who views source — that is
# fine for a Turnstile sitekey, which is designed to be public, and is why the
# matching SECRET is not here. Secrets live on the Worker:
#
#     cd site
#     CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN="$CF_API_TOKEN" npx wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY
#     CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN="$CF_API_TOKEN" npx wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY
#
# Never put a secret in this file, in .env, or in wrangler.jsonc "vars".

# Cloudflare Turnstile sitekey for the widget on every form.
#
# Create the widget at Cloudflare dashboard > Turnstile. Widget mode:
# "Invisible". Its allowed hostnames must list EVERY hostname the site is served
# on, or the token verifies nowhere and every submission is refused:
#
#     staging-lp-rexdalemobilewash.ash-47a.workers.dev   (the staging Worker)
#     lp.rexdalemobilewash.ca                            (once the domain moves)
#     www.lp.rexdalemobilewash.ca
#
# Build without this set and the forms render no widget and refuse everything —
# by design, since the endpoints fail closed. The build prints a warning saying
# so rather than failing.
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY=

# --- Testing keys -----------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare publishes sitekey/secret pairs with fixed outcomes. bin/prove-bot-
# protection.mjs uses them so the proof exercises the real siteverify API
# without a real widget. Never deploy with these.
#
#   always passes   sitekey 1x00000000000000000000AA
#                   secret  1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
#   always blocks   sitekey 2x00000000000000000000AB
#                   secret  2x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
#   token always spent      secret 3x0000000000000000000000000000000AA
